IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 6A -- THE UNITED KINGDOM'S FINANCIAL INTELLIGENCE UNIT (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3349-3390 of the plain-text
-- rendering, which is not the official text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  The NCA (National Crime Agency) is the UK's financial intelligence unit (FIU).  This Schedule says how the
-- NCA deals with the FIUs of other EEA states: it answers their requests for information, may ask a relevant person (a bank,
-- an accountancy firm) for information in order to answer them, asks them in turn about a relevant person whose head office is
-- abroad, and keeps within the limits they place on what it receives.  Every duty here is the NCA's, except the duty of a UK
-- competent authority to report to the NCA (paragraph 2).  Nothing in it gives a relevant person a right or imposes a duty on one;
-- what it means to a relevant person is that the NCA MAY seek an order for information from it (paragraph 5(a)) and that a request
-- about it with its head office in another EEA state goes to that state's FIU (paragraph 14).  The seat questions are those two.
--
-- THE PARAGRAPH NUMBERS (FORK S6A-F1).  The rendering prints the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 13 and 16 and leaves the other
-- paragraphs bare.  The numbers used here are fixed by the Schedule's own cross-references: "subject to paragraph 10" (lines 3365,
-- 3368) is the paragraph that begins "Where an obligation arises" (line 3374); "subject to paragraph 11" and "under paragraph 7"
-- (lines 3370, 3375) fix the consent duty (3370) as 7 and the exception (3375) as 11; "paragraphs 14 and 15" (line 3383) fix the two
-- paragraphs after paragraph 13.  This gives: 1 = 3350-3359; 2 = 3361; 3 = 3363; 4 = 3365; 5 = 3366-3368; 6 = 3369; 7 = 3370; 8 = 3371;
-- 9 = 3373; 10 = 3374; 11 = 3375-3377; 12 = 3378-3381; 13 = 3383; 14 = 3384; 15 = 3385; 16 = 3387-3390.
--
-- DUTIES AND PERMISSIONS ARE ENCODED TWICE.  For each paragraph that says the NCA (or a UK competent authority) "must" or "may" do
-- something there is (1) a decision function that says whether the duty or permission ARISES on the facts, and (2) a regulative
-- rule, `PARTY ... MUST/MAY ...`, that returns the duty when the decision function says JUST TRUE (and FULFILLED, no duty, when it says anything else).
-- The decision function is JUST TRUE when the duty arises; JUST FALSE ("the duty does not arise on these facts") when a "where", "upon request" or "apply where"
-- that the paragraph states is not met (Meng's rulings of 2026-11-05: a "where" not met answers JUST FALSE like "if"; "upon", "when" and "whenever" count as "where");
-- and NOTHING when the paragraph states a scope with no such word ("In response to an external request" in paragraph 4, "provided in response to an external request" in
-- paragraph 9, "foreign FIUs" in paragraph 3) or a "(subject to paragraph 10 / 11)" exception (the paragraph is limited by its own wording, and has no "only").  The text gives no number of days
-- ("promptly", "upon request"), so the rules carry no WITHIN (FORK S6A-F4).
-- Where the NCA's own consideration decides the matter ("could be contrary to national law", "considers") the consideration is a
-- BOOLEAN fact: the NCA's judgment is an input, never computed.

-- src:3349 | SCHEDULE 6A — The United Kingdom’s Financial Intelligence Unit
§ `Schedule 6A -- The United Kingdom's Financial Intelligence Unit`

DECLARE `sch 6A party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6A the NCA`
    `sch 6A a United Kingdom competent authority`

DECLARE `sch 6A act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6A provide a report to the NCA about the authority's use of the information, including the outcome of any investigations or inspections`
    `sch 6A take such steps as the NCA considers appropriate to co-operate with foreign FIUs`
    `sch 6A provide promptly any relevant information in the NCA's possession`
    `sch 6A exercise the powers to seek an order for information from the relevant person`
    `sch 6A provide promptly to the foreign FIU the relevant information received in consequence of the order`
    `sch 6A designate at least one point of contact with responsibility for receiving external requests`
    `sch 6A consent to the dissemination of as much of the requested information as possible and communicate the consent promptly`
    `sch 6A take such steps as the NCA considers appropriate to ensure the information is transmitted securely`
    `sch 6A impose such restrictions and conditions on the use of the information as the NCA considers appropriate`
    `sch 6A decide not to provide some or all of the information`
    `sch 6A have particular regard to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information as possible`
    `sch 6A have particular regard to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information by the foreign FIU as possible`
    `sch 6A address the request for the information to the foreign FIU in the state in which the relevant person has its head office`
    `sch 6A put in the request the relevant facts and background information, the reasons for the request and how the information is proposed to be used`
    `sch 6A use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided`
    `sch 6A comply with the restrictions or conditions of use imposed by the foreign FIU`
    `sch 6A obtain the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any further dissemination of the information`

DECLARE `sch 6A para 1 defined Act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6A para 1 the 2000 Act`
    `sch 6A para 1 the 2002 Act`

-- Paragraph 1: the definitions of the Schedule.  Each is a "means" definition, so a case outside it is the text's no.
-- src:3350 | 1 Interpretation
-- src:3351 | In this Schedule
-- src:3352 | “external request” means a request to the NCA for information by a foreign FIU which may be relevant for the purpose of the foreign FIU’s performance of FIU functions;
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3350-3352)
GIVEN `the request is made to the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information requested may be relevant for the foreign FIU's performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 1 the request is an external request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request is made to the NCA` AND `the request is made by a foreign FIU` AND `the information requested may be relevant for the foreign FIU's performance of FIU functions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“external request” means a request to the NCA for information by a foreign FIU which may be relevant for the purpose of the foreign FIU’s performance of FIU functions;"


-- src:3353 | “FIU functions” means the functions of a financial intelligence unit as set out in the fourth money laundering directive;
-- "FIU functions" are defined by pointing at the fourth money laundering directive, which is not among the sources.
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3353)
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 6A para 1 FIU functions are` MEANS "the functions of a financial intelligence unit as set out in the fourth money laundering directive"


-- src:3354 | “foreign competent authority” means an authority in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom which has equivalent functions to those of a United Kingdom competent authority to which a foreign FIU may provide information in connection with its performance of FIU functions;
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3354)
GIVEN `the authority is in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has functions equivalent to those of a United Kingdom competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a foreign FIU may provide information to the authority in connection with its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 1 the authority is a foreign competent authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority is in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` AND `the authority has functions equivalent to those of a United Kingdom competent authority` AND `a foreign FIU may provide information to the authority in connection with its performance of FIU functions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign competent authority” means an authority in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom which has equivalent functions to those of a United Kingdom competent authority to which a foreign FIU may provide information in connection with its performance of FIU functions;"


-- src:3355 | “foreign FIU” means an authority in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom which performs FIU functions in that state;
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3355)
GIVEN `the authority is in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority performs FIU functions in that state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 1 the authority is a foreign FIU` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the authority is in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` AND `the authority performs FIU functions in that state`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign FIU” means an authority in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom which performs FIU functions in that state;"


-- src:3356 | “relevant information” means information the NCA possesses in connection with its performance of FIU functions which it considers relevant to an external request;
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3356)
GIVEN `the NCA possesses the information in connection with its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers the information relevant to an external request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 1 the information is relevant information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA possesses the information in connection with its performance of FIU functions` AND `the NCA considers the information relevant to an external request`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant information” means information the NCA possesses in connection with its performance of FIU functions which it considers relevant to an external request;"


-- src:3357 | “the 2000 Act” means the Terrorism Act 2000 ;
-- src:3358 | “the 2002 Act” means the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ;
-- "the 2000 Act" and "the 2002 Act" are pointers at other Acts, which are not among the sources.
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3357-3358)
GIVEN act IS A `sch 6A para 1 defined Act`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 6A para 1 the defined Act is` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `sch 6A para 1 the 2000 Act` THEN "the Terrorism Act 2000"
    WHEN `sch 6A para 1 the 2002 Act` THEN "the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002"


-- src:3359 | “United Kingdom competent authority” means any authority other than the NCA concerned in the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences contained in Part 7 (money laundering) of the 2002 Act or Part 3 (terrorist property) of the 2000 Act, and any supervisory authority, to which the NCA disseminates information in its performance of FIU functions.
-- "any authority other than the NCA concerned in the prevention ... of criminal offences ..., and any supervisory authority, to which the NCA disseminates
-- information in its performance of FIU functions".  "Other than the NCA" is read to qualify the first kind only; "to which the NCA disseminates" both (FORK S6A-F2).
@ref sch 6A para 1 (src:3359)
GIVEN `the body is the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is concerned in the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences contained in Part 7 (money laundering) of the 2002 Act or Part 3 (terrorist property) of the 2000 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA disseminates information to the body in its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 1 the body is a United Kingdom competent authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (    ((NOT `the body is the NCA`) AND `the body is concerned in the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences contained in Part 7 (money laundering) of the 2002 Act or Part 3 (terrorist property) of the 2000 Act`)
                 OR `the body is a supervisory authority`)
           AND `the NCA disseminates information to the body in its performance of FIU functions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“United Kingdom competent authority” means any authority other than the NCA concerned in the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences contained in Part 7 (money laundering) of the 2002 Act or Part 3 (terrorist property) of the 2000 Act, and any supervisory authority, to which the NCA disseminates information in its performance of FIU functions."


-- src:3360 | 2 Reports to the National Crime Agency
-- src:3361 | Where the NCA has, in its performance of FIU functions, disseminated any information to a United Kingdom competent authority, that authority must, upon request, provide a report to the NCA about the authority’s use of that information, including the outcome of any investigations or inspections conducted on the basis of that information.
@ref sch 6A para 2 (src:3360-3361)
GIVEN `the NCA has disseminated information to the authority in its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is a United Kingdom competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has requested a report from the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 2 the authority must provide a report to the NCA` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA has disseminated information to the authority in its performance of FIU functions` AND `the authority is a United Kingdom competent authority` AND `the NCA has requested a report from the authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA has, in its performance of FIU functions, disseminated any information to a United Kingdom competent authority, that authority must, upon request, provide a report to the NCA" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 2 (src:3360-3361)
GIVEN `the NCA has disseminated information to the authority in its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is a United Kingdom competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has requested a report from the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 2 the report duty` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 2 the authority must provide a report to the NCA` `the NCA has disseminated information to the authority in its performance of FIU functions` `the authority is a United Kingdom competent authority` `the NCA has requested a report from the authority`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A a United Kingdom competent authority`
         MUST `sch 6A provide a report to the NCA about the authority's use of the information, including the outcome of any investigations or inspections`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3362 | 3 Co-operation
-- src:3363 | The NCA must take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with foreign FIUs in their performance of FIU functions.
@ref sch 6A para 3 (src:3362-3363)
GIVEN `the other body is a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 3 the NCA must take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with the foreign FIU` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the other body is a foreign FIU`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph states when the duty arises and does not say that it does not arise in another case

@ref sch 6A para 3 (src:3362-3363)
GIVEN `the other body is a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 3 the co-operation duty` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 3 the NCA must take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with the foreign FIU` `the other body is a foreign FIU`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A take such steps as the NCA considers appropriate to co-operate with foreign FIUs`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3364 | 4 Provision of information in response to external requests
-- src:3365 | In response to an external request, the NCA must (subject to paragraph 10) provide promptly any relevant information in the NCA’s possession.
@ref sch 6A para 4 (src:3364-3365)
GIVEN `the request is an external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA possesses relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 4 the NCA must provide promptly any relevant information in its possession` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request is an external request` AND `the NCA possesses relevant information` AND (NOT `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph states when the duty arises and does not say that it does not arise in another case

@ref sch 6A para 4 (src:3364-3365)
GIVEN `the request is an external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA possesses relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 4 the duty to provide information` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 4 the NCA must provide promptly any relevant information in its possession` `the request is an external request` `the NCA possesses relevant information` `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A provide promptly any relevant information in the NCA's possession`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- Paragraph 5: the lead-in (line 3366) applies to both limbs; the three facts are the lead-in's conditions.
-- src:3366 | Where an external request is received and the NCA does not possess information which the NCA considers relevant to the external request, and it suspects a relevant person possesses such information, the NCA—
-- src:3367 | (a) may exercise its powers under Parts 7 and 8 (investigations) of the 2002 Act, any orders made under section 445 (external investigations) of that Act, or Part 3 of the 2000 Act , as applicable, to seek an order for information from such person, and
-- src:3368 | (b) must (subject to paragraph 10) provide any relevant information received in consequence of any such order promptly to the foreign FIU concerned.
@ref sch 6A para 5 (src:3366-3368)
GIVEN `an external request is received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 5(a) the NCA may exercise its powers to seek an order for information from the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an external request is received` AND `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` AND `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an external request is received and the NCA does not possess information which the NCA considers relevant to the external request, and it suspects a relevant person possesses such information" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 5 (src:3366-3367)
GIVEN `an external request is received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 5(a) the power to seek an order` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 5(a) the NCA may exercise its powers to seek an order for information from the relevant person` `an external request is received` `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MAY `sch 6A exercise the powers to seek an order for information from the relevant person`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref sch 6A para 5 (src:3366-3368)
GIVEN `an external request is received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has received relevant information in consequence of an order sought under paragraph 5(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 5(b) the NCA must provide to the foreign FIU the relevant information received in consequence of an order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an external request is received` AND `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` AND `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` AND `the NCA has received relevant information in consequence of an order sought under paragraph 5(a)` AND (NOT `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (`an external request is received` AND `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` AND `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an external request is received and the NCA does not possess information which the NCA considers relevant to the external request, and it suspects a relevant person possesses such information" is not met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph states when the duty arises and does not say that it does not arise in another case

@ref sch 6A para 5 (src:3366-3368)
GIVEN `an external request is received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has received relevant information in consequence of an order sought under paragraph 5(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 5(b) the duty to pass on the information received` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 5(b) the NCA must provide to the foreign FIU the relevant information received in consequence of an order` `an external request is received` `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` `the NCA has received relevant information in consequence of an order sought under paragraph 5(a)` `the NCA has decided under paragraph 10 not to provide the information`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A provide promptly to the foreign FIU the relevant information received in consequence of the order`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3369 | The NCA must designate at least one point of contact with responsibility for receiving external requests.
@ref sch 6A para 6 (src:3369)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 6 the NCA must designate at least one point of contact` MEANS
    JUST TRUE -- the paragraph has no condition: the NCA must designate at least one point of contact

@ref sch 6A para 6 (src:3369)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 6 the duty to designate a point of contact` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
    MUST `sch 6A designate at least one point of contact with responsibility for receiving external requests`


-- src:3370 | Where the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU, and that foreign FIU makes a request for consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority, the NCA must (subject to paragraph 11) consent to the dissemination of as much of the requested information as possible and communicate its consent promptly to the foreign FIU.
-- "(subject to paragraph 11)": the duty does not arise where paragraph 11 applies (the two facts PREJ and CONTRARY).  Paragraph 11 limits the duty "if and to the extent"; this function answers whether any duty arises, and the extent is the NCA's own consideration (an input).
@ref sch 6A para 7 (src:3370)
GIVEN `the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign FIU has requested consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 7 the NCA must consent to the dissemination of the requested information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU` AND `the foreign FIU has requested consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority` AND (NOT `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)`) AND (NOT `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (`the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU` AND `the foreign FIU has requested consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU, and that foreign FIU makes a request for consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority" is not met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph states when the duty arises and does not say that it does not arise in another case

@ref sch 6A para 7 (src:3370)
GIVEN `the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign FIU has requested consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 7 the duty to consent to dissemination` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 7 the NCA must consent to the dissemination of the requested information` `the NCA has provided relevant information to a foreign FIU` `the foreign FIU has requested consent to disseminate some or all of the relevant information to a foreign competent authority` `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)` `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A consent to the dissemination of as much of the requested information as possible and communicate the consent promptly`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3371 | Where the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule, the NCA shall take such steps as it considers appropriate to ensure that such information is transmitted securely.
@ref sch 6A para 8 (src:3371)
GIVEN `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 8 the NCA shall take such steps as it considers appropriate to ensure the information is transmitted securely` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 8 (src:3371)
GIVEN `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 8 the duty to transmit securely` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 8 the NCA shall take such steps as it considers appropriate to ensure the information is transmitted securely` `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A take such steps as the NCA considers appropriate to ensure the information is transmitted securely`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3372 | 9 Conditions and restrictions on provision or further dissemination of relevant information
-- src:3373 | The NCA may impose such restrictions and conditions on the use of relevant information provided in response to an external request as the NCA considers appropriate.
@ref sch 6A para 9 (src:3372-3373)
GIVEN `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 9 the NCA may impose restrictions and conditions on the use of the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph states when the permission arises and does not say that it does not arise in another case

@ref sch 6A para 9 (src:3372-3373)
GIVEN `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 9 the power to impose restrictions and conditions` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 9 the NCA may impose restrictions and conditions on the use of the information` `the NCA provides relevant information in response to an external request in accordance with this Schedule`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MAY `sch 6A impose such restrictions and conditions on the use of the information as the NCA considers appropriate`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3374 | Where an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request, the NCA may decide not to provide some or all of the information where and to the extent that the NCA considers that doing so could be contrary to national law.
-- "where and to the extent that the NCA considers": the NCA's consideration is the fact; the extent to which it may decline follows it and is not computed.
@ref sch 6A para 10 (src:3374)
GIVEN `an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that providing the information could be contrary to national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 10 the NCA may decide not to provide some or all of the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request` AND `the NCA considers that providing the information could be contrary to national law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request, the NCA may decide not to provide some or all of the information where and to the extent that the NCA considers that doing so could be contrary to national law" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 10 (src:3374)
GIVEN `an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that providing the information could be contrary to national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 10 the power to decide not to provide information` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 10 the NCA may decide not to provide some or all of the information` `an obligation arises under this Schedule for the NCA to provide relevant information in response to an external request` `the NCA considers that providing the information could be contrary to national law`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MAY `sch 6A decide not to provide some or all of the information`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3375 | The NCA is not required to comply with the duty to give consent to the dissemination of information to a foreign competent authority under paragraph 7 if and to the extent that the NCA considers that the giving of such consent could—
-- src:3376 | (a) prejudice an investigation, whether into a criminal cause or matter or in relation to any investigation referred to in section 341 (investigations) of the 2002 Act or to which Schedule 5A (terrorist financing investigations) to the 2000 Act applies; or
-- src:3377 | (b) be contrary to national law.
-- Paragraph 11: "The NCA is not required to comply with the duty ... under paragraph 7 if and to the extent that the NCA considers that the giving of such consent could (a) ... or (b) ...".
-- A flat negative with an "if": it is the text's no for the case it names.  "To the extent" is the NCA's own consideration (an input).
@ref sch 6A para 11 (src:3375-3377)
GIVEN `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 11 the NCA is required to give the consent under paragraph 7` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA considers that giving the consent could prejudice an investigation of a kind described in paragraph 11(a)` OR `the NCA considers that giving the consent could be contrary to national law`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The NCA is not required to comply with the duty to give consent to the dissemination of information to a foreign competent authority under paragraph 7 if and to the extent that the NCA considers that the giving of such consent could— (a) prejudice an investigation ...; or (b) be contrary to national law."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph removes the duty in the two cases it names; whether the duty arises in another case is paragraph 7


-- src:3378 | The NCA must have particular regard—
-- src:3379 | (a) where making a decision under paragraph 10, to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information in response to external requests as possible, or
-- src:3380 | (b) where making a decision under paragraph 11, to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information as possible by a foreign FIU to foreign competent authorities,
-- src:3381 | in order for the foreign FIU concerned to carry out FIU functions efficiently and effectively.
@ref sch 6A para 12 (src:3378-3381)
GIVEN `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 12(a) the NCA must have particular regard to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information as possible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 10`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where making a decision under paragraph 10, to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information in response to external requests as possible" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 12 (src:3378-3379)
GIVEN `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 12(a) the duty to have regard to the exchange of information` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 12(a) the NCA must have particular regard to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information as possible` `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 10`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A have particular regard to the need for as unfettered an exchange of relevant information as possible`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref sch 6A para 12 (src:3378-3381)
GIVEN `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 12(b) the NCA must have particular regard to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information by the foreign FIU as possible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 11`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where making a decision under paragraph 11, to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information as possible by a foreign FIU to foreign competent authorities" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 12 (src:3378-3381)
GIVEN `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 12(b) the duty to have regard to dissemination` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 12(b) the NCA must have particular regard to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information by the foreign FIU as possible` `the NCA is making a decision under paragraph 11`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A have particular regard to the need for as unfettered dissemination of information by the foreign FIU as possible`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3382 | 13 Requests for information by the NCA to foreign FIUs
-- src:3383 | Paragraphs 14 and 15 apply where the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person which has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 6A para 13 (src:3382-3383)
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 13 paragraphs 14 and 15 apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` AND `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs 14 and 15 apply where the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person which has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom" is not met


-- src:3384 | The NCA must address a request for the information to the foreign FIU in the state in which the relevant person has its head office.
@ref sch 6A para 14 (src:3384)
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 14 the NCA must address the request to the foreign FIU in the state of the head office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` AND `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs 14 and 15 apply where the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person which has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom (paragraph 13)" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 14 (src:3384)
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 14 the duty to address the request to the foreign FIU` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 14 the NCA must address the request to the foreign FIU in the state of the head office` `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A address the request for the information to the foreign FIU in the state in which the relevant person has its head office`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3385 | Where the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information which the NCA considers may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions, the request must contain the relevant facts and background information, reasons for the request and how the information sought is proposed to be used.
-- Paragraph 13 says paragraphs 14 and 15 "apply where" the NCA wishes to obtain information about a relevant person with its head office in another EEA state; paragraph 15 is read with that limit (FORK S6A-F3).
@ref sch 6A para 15 (src:3385)
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 15 the request must contain the relevant facts, the reasons and the proposed use` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` AND `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` AND `the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information` AND `the NCA considers that the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information which the NCA considers may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions, and paragraph 13: Paragraphs 14 and 15 apply where the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person which has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 15 (src:3385)
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA considers that the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 15 the duty on the content of the request` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 15 the request must contain the relevant facts, the reasons and the proposed use` `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` `the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information` `the NCA considers that the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A put in the request the relevant facts and background information, the reasons for the request and how the information is proposed to be used`
    ELSE FULFILLED


-- src:3386 | 16 Conditions and restrictions on use of information received by the NCA from foreign FIUs
-- src:3387 | Where the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU, the NCA must—
-- src:3388 | (a) use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided, unless it has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any other use of the information;
-- src:3389 | (b) comply with any restrictions or conditions of use which have been imposed by the foreign FIU in respect of the information; and
-- src:3390 | (c) obtain the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any further dissemination of the information.
@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3390)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to another use of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 16(a) the NCA must use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` AND `the NCA has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to another use of the information`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided, unless it has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any other use of the information"
        IF `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3388)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the NCA has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to another use of the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 16(a) the duty to use the information only for its purpose` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 16(a) the NCA must use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided` `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` `the NCA has obtained the prior consent of the foreign FIU to another use of the information`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A use the information only for the purpose for which it was sought or provided`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3389)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 16(b) the NCA must comply with the restrictions or conditions of use imposed by the foreign FIU` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3389)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 16(b) the duty to comply with the foreign FIU's restrictions` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 16(b) the NCA must comply with the restrictions or conditions of use imposed by the foreign FIU` `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A comply with the restrictions or conditions of use imposed by the foreign FIU`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3390)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6A para 16(c) the NCA must obtain the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any further dissemination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU" is not met

@ref sch 6A para 16 (src:3386-3390)
GIVEN `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 6A party` `sch 6A act`
`sch 6A para 16(c) the duty to obtain consent to further dissemination` MEANS
    IF (`sch 6A para 16(c) the NCA must obtain the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any further dissemination` `the NCA receives information from a foreign FIU`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `sch 6A the NCA`
         MUST `sch 6A obtain the prior consent of the foreign FIU to any further dissemination of the information`
    ELSE FULFILLED


